The function is already minimal, so the only change is a branch hint. The common case, where the field already holds its type, is laid out as the fall-through path. Behavior is identical for every input.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    if ((profile == NULL) || (profileIndex >= profile->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return profile->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```